203
00:22:21,935 --> 00:22:29,458
We explored over the last year whether we could maybe partner with a preservation restriction.

204
00:22:29,518 --> 00:22:33,140
Let me back up because not all of you may be familiar with preservation restrictions.

205
00:22:33,660 --> 00:22:46,192
Preservation restrictions are a deed restriction that provides long-term or perpetual protections of the historic elements of those properties.

206
00:22:46,432 --> 00:22:56,261
Any improvement or change to the property would have to be approved by the body who holds that deed restriction.

207
00:22:57,022 --> 00:23:06,970
And so the city of Medford cannot hold deed restrictions on its own property because we would not be able to enforce a deed restriction on our own property.

208
00:23:07,030 --> 00:23:10,793
We need another organization or entity to hold that deed restriction.

209
00:23:11,513 --> 00:23:21,541
So as it says right now in the plan, there are very few organizations who will do this, private organizations, and it's very expensive when they do.

210
00:23:23,542 --> 00:23:27,003
It's very complicated and challenging.

211
00:23:27,023 --> 00:23:42,588
An alternative, an option that we had explored last year was to see whether the city of Somerville might partner with Medford to have an exchange to hold each other's preservation restrictions.

212
00:23:43,148 --> 00:23:50,310
Many years ago, Somerville had explored this with Medford and we weren't open to it at the time, but times may have changed.

213
00:23:53,946 --> 00:24:02,592
Now that we're looking at this as a potential good idea to meet our need, Somerville was not particularly receptive.

214
00:24:06,012 --> 00:24:14,156
So I'm not sure whether we can find enough interest on both sides at the same time to be able to make this happen.

215
00:24:14,656 --> 00:24:27,002
But another option that I see happening in Somerville that might be able to resolve that problem would be to create local historic districts.

216
00:24:28,269 --> 00:24:43,965
for the city-owned historic properties, and then the approvals that are required for local historic districts would apply to the city-owned properties.

217
00:24:44,045 --> 00:24:49,850
